      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ui): create catalog sessions from the sidebar",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users could not start provider-native sessions from a session catalog header, and where a Claude Code session created through OpenClaw appeared twice: once under Claude Code and again under the owning agent's Chats group.\n\nThe existing sidebar also made agent ownership difficult to scan because nested session rows lacked a clear hierarchy and session creation was detached from the agent it targeted.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds an optional catalog-provided session creation capability and routes the Claude Code header action through the existing `/new` workflow, preserving agent, model, folder, worktree, and execution-node choices. It also places creation actions on agent rows, adds accessible hierarchy rails, and links Claude CLI-backed OpenClaw sessions to their catalog entries so they render only once.\n\nThe backing OpenClaw session remains intact for execution; only its duplicate sidebar presentation is suppressed.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can now:\n\n- create a session directly from an agent row or the Claude Code catalog header;\n- retain the normal new-session location and execution controls;\n- see clearer agent-to-session ownership in the sidebar; and\n- see Claude Code sessions only under Claude Code instead of duplicated under main Chats.\n\nSingle-agent behavior remains unchanged, and the hierarchy uses logical CSS properties for RTL layouts.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- 58 focused protocol, Anthropic catalog, sidebar, location, and create-parameter tests passed.\n- 8 focused gateway catalog method tests passed across the gateway test projects.\n- All 7 new-session browser E2E tests passed.\n- `pnpm tsgo` passed.\n- Oxlint passed on all changed TypeScript files.\n- Oxfmt passed on all changed TypeScript and CSS files.\n- Full `pnpm build` passed after rebasing onto current `upstream/main`.\n",
        "branch": "fix/sidebar-agent-session-hierarchy",
